WEBVTT

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:04.230
I won't give up!

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.280
Luna!

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.890
Bell!

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.310
Luna!

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.550
Stop it!

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.940
Will you stop already?

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:18.750
But!

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.060
It's no use! It's too dangerous!

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.640
Luna!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.700
Luna fell into the sea!

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:25.640
What'd he say?

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.140
Set course to sixty degrees astern!

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:27.660
Kaoru!

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.530
I know!

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.890
The rudder won't work!

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.160
That's...

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.960
Luna!

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.610
Why aren't we following her?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.160
We've lost sight of Luna!

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.490
The rudder won't work because of the storm.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.380
I didn't think we'd have this bad a storm!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:53.990
Where's Luna?

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.550
Adam, what about Luna's voice?

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.650
I can't hear it. I can't hear it!

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.810
Luna...

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.840
Is Luna going to die?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:04.000
Is she?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.060
Luna...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.710
...won't die!

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.740
That's right. She definitely won't die!

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.400
Luna wouldn't be killed by a storm like this!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.090
Everyone, have faith!

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.640
Have faith, and hope for Luna's safety!

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.750
Good luck, Luna!

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.900
Live.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.310
I can't... Dad...

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.940
Live, Luna!

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.800
I won't give up.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:12.360
I won't give up, Dad!

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.730
As if I'd let myself give up!

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.690
I'm... alive...

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.350
I'm... saved.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.410
I wonder if everyone's safe.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.790
Adam, can you hear me?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.810
No use.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.190
Water...

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:38.240
There's no fruit, no river, no anything.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.660
It's no use.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:03.930
I don't have a moment to waste in sending a signal so they know I'm here.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:19.150
If I'd known this would happen, I would have had Bell show me how to start a fire.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.250
I'm so hungry that I have no strength.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.090
It stings!

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:58.380
I have to sharpen the tip.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:00.510
A stone...

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:02.240
...a stone..

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.460
A stone that can cut wood...

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:07.410
There isn't one.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.250
No choice.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.190
Nothing I can do.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.400
No choice but to try with this.

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:24.960
Maybe...

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.190
Water...

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:32.430
No use.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.550
Why you...

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.650
I did it! I did it!

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.260
Ouch!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.440
No use.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.100
That's right!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.230
They used this method in old movies...

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.040
It caught!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:32.200
It's fire...

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:33.890
It's fire!

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.730
I wonder how everyone is right now.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.540
Hopefully they've noticed this fire.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.150
Luna...

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:29.910
Who is it?

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.910
Luna...

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.200
Dad?

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:37.600
Luna.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.910
Come to think of it, a long time ago...

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.790
...I watched a bonfire with Dad like this once.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.650
This is my first bonfire!

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.260
Actually, it's mine too.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.250
Really?

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.530
Is it okay?

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.300
Havin' an open fire in the colony.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:20.760
This is an vegetation experiment plant cut off from the residence area.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.110
It's special.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.190
I wanted to try it once.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:31.600
Because our ancestors sat around fires like this for thousands of years.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:36.810
Just by watching it like this, I feel like my heart gets warmer.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.840
It's just 'cuz the fire's hot.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.610
No, I feel relieved!

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.350
I feel that way too.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.430
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:52.790
Well, thanks to this thick, dense forest, humanity can survive here.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.660
I dunno if human bodies are mysterious or just infathomable.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:02.580
Hey Daddy, you and your friends made this whole forest?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.230
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:10.790
We tilled the soil, planted the seedlings, gave them water and fertilizer, and made them this big.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:15.510
Because plants make the oxygen humans need.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.080
This is what they call, "Terraforming."

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:20.430
Terraforming?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:26.050
To put it simply, it's making a planet's environment inhabitable for us humans.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:32.910
This place is in the midst of terraforming, which will take many years.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:40.900
And when it's finished, people will be able to live anywhere like on Earth, instead of just in colonies.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.950
So that's Daddy's job! That's amazing!

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.250
Daddy, is something wrong?

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:55.900
I take pride in my work, but...

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:00.210
Sometimes... I have a thought.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:05.840
Considering the number of planets in the universe,

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:11.950
maybe changing planets other than Earth so that humans can live on them is arrogant.

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:16.380
Maybe, but Earth doesn't have an environment where humans can live anymore.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:19.750
If you don't do this, humanity'd go extinct.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:27.550
That's right. Even though I assure myself of that, sometimes that thought comes into my head.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.250
I don't really understand.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.810
Maybe it's a bit early to talk to you about that, Luna.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:38.090
Got that right. She still wets the bed so much you could draw a map of space with it.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:40.080
I do <i>not</i> wet the bed!

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.190
Then who helps you clean up after?

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:45.590
You promised you'd never tell!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:49.150
And you didn't gimme the juice you promised!

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.330
What?

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.490
Wha'?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.140
Okay, stop fighting now.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.490
I'd be happy if you could get along.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.290
We won't get along!

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:08.650
Luna, do you know?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.740
How many stars there are in the galaxy.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.860
Maybe about a hundred?

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.950
They say there's over two hundred billion just in this galaxy.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.160
Two hundred billion?

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.360
One, ten, hundred, thousand, ten-thousand...

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:30.250
...hundred-thousand, million, ten-million, hundred-million...

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.630
That many?

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:40.390
And there are scholars who say there's at least ten million planets in the galaxy

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:43.980
just like old earth with water and life.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.410
Ten million... that's so many!

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:54.700
Out of so many stars, only that many have life.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.840
How romantic!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:00.030
Space is super, <i>super</i> huge!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:08.050
So compared to the size of space, this planet where we live is the size of a grain of sand.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.480
Grain of sand?

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.750
But many people live here.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:22.190
So what we're doing, relative to the vastness of space, is just an incomparably small thing...

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.830
...but on these worlds where there is no life...

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:29.830
...I work frantically because I want to cultivate the tree of life, even if it's just a little at a time.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.740
That's how your dad feels, Luna.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.400
Tree of life?

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.810
What a wonderful phrase!

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.530
Hey, hey. Don't say it carelessly.

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:44.950
Chako, shut up!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.260
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:52.710
When I'm grown up, I want to be a planetary settlement engineer just like you, Daddy!

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:54.030
Really?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.400
Then you'd better study really hard.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:16:59.500
I'll do my best!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.590
Dad...

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.660
...I've done my best since then.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:15.400
I've studied all I can so I can be a planetary settlement engineer.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.250
I want...

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:20.840
...my Mom...

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.010
...and Dad...

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.810
...to praise my hard work...

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.630
The cut is gone!

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.200
The blisters are gone too.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.000
Water...

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:32.050
No use after all.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.240
Morning dew!

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.560
If I don't hurry, it'll evaporate!

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:04.300
I have to eat something.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.180
Water...

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.710
I want to drink like crazy.

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:05.760
I have to conserve my strength as much as I can.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.110
I have to wake up earlier tomorrow...

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.030
...and drink...

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:17.500
...more...dew...

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:05.350
Fall! Fall! Fall faster!

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.960
Come to think of it, Dad said that too.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:12.660
Nature is very harsh, very kind...

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:16.340
...and very beautiful.

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.030
Luna!

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:43.600
Everyone!

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:47.500
Hey!

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:51.290
Everyone! Hey!

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:08.430
The reason Luna's wounds healed so quickly is because a certain substance is in her body.

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:12.630
'Cuz of that, Luna's anxious and in low spirits.

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:13.750
What should we do?

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:19.040
How about we have a party
to try make Luna a little happier?

00:23:19.600 --> 00:23:21.740
Hit the nail on the head as usual.

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:23.200
Good idea, Sharla!

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:24.740
Okay, let's get started!

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:28.380
Next time: Why is something like that...
